WEBVTT

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.580
Natsusa!

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.750
Madoka-<i>san</i>! Thank you for coming.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:26.330
"Koufuuin Fourth Year College Student"
"Madoka Hongou" "Number 15, Full Back"
Good job. Have you gotten
used to being a manager?

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:28.660
Yes. I'm slowly getting used to it.

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:31.620
Madoka-<i>san</i>, thank you for--

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:35.950
Um, sorry. Please only do <i>kabe-don </i>when
there's an actual wall to do it against.

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:39.540
"Koufuuin Third Year College Student"
"Kazutaka Hongou" "Number 8, Number 8"
Don't you have something to say to me?

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:41.910
Huh? What?

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:43.000
Oh! Are you talking about the fact that
your nickname "forward god of destruction"

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.410
"The God of Backs" "Madoka Hongou"
"The Forward God of Destruction" "Kazutaka Hongou"
Oh! Are you talking about the fact that
your nickname "forward god of destruction"

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:49.160
"The God of Backs" "Madoka Hongou"
"The Forward God of Destruction" "Kazutaka Hongou"
is so unbelievably uncool that
I make fun of it behind your back?

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:52.370
You have a lot of guts.

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:54.870
Those two are still the same.

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:57.580
Koufuuin has a match after this right?

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:03.620
That's right. More importantly, Natsusa.
This is bad. Since you can't win against us,

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:07.160
you're going to drop out of the
Kansai league if you lose again.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:11.080
Why are you so sure that we'd lose against you?

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:14.080
I mean, your team didn't win
against us these last two years.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:19.910
But those players have already graduated,
and you're the captain this year...

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:22.290
So, we might be able to win.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.040
Aw, Natsusa.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:28.080
You used to be so cute,
but you've gotten really cocky lately.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:29.410
Ouch!

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:30.830
Well, whatever.

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:36.160
Even if you lose in the Kansai league,
come cheer us on in Chichibunomiya.

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:40.580
Kazutaka, we're leaving.

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:43.620
You better prepare yourself for the final match.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:49.660
I'll make you regret the fact you gave up
once on rugby without my permission.

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:52.080
What the hell is up with those brothers?!

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:54.750
Was our high school just
brimming with sadistic people?

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.620
I'm pretty sadistic myself,
but I never get a chance to show it.

00:01:57.620 --> 00:01:59.540
Putting their personalities aside,

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:03.200
Koufuuin is the strongest they have ever been.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.450
The chances of losing
in the finals is really high.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:09.160
We have to win the next
match no matter what

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:11.750
or we'll lose our chance
to go to the nationals.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:16.700
Tsuru.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.120
"Regression is also evolution."
Shit! How did things turn out this way?!

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:58.910
Huh?

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:01.870
Recover by the preseason match next week.

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:04.330
Otherwise, we'll remove you
from the starting line-up.

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:09.370
Yasunari was terrible today.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:14.910
Doesn't it piss you off that he dropped so
many of the balls you recovered, Fuuga?

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.250
Well...

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:18.620
It can't be helped.

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:23.120
It used to be Natsusa's position.
Yasunari is under a lot of pressure.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:27.040
By the way, wasn't the number 14
on the other team really similar to Natsusa?

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:29.040
He was! He was like an exact copy.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.370
Yasunari completely lost against him.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:35.620
It would have been impossible for him
to be a starting member if Natsusa was here.

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:39.080
That's true. That guy was really lucky.

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:41.120
You bastards! What'd you just say?!

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:43.040
Yasunari! Stop!

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:45.250
The truth.

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:49.080
Don't be so cocky, trade-in.

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:53.160
Kotori! Apologize!

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:55.290
--Stop!
--Let go!

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:57.120
Stop it, Kotori!

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:59.120
Hey! What's going on?!

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:01.290
Natsu-<i>senpai</i>!

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:02.580
What happened?

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:04.830
--That guy!
--Don't get yourself involved!

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:07.080
No, I normally should in this situation.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:10.080
It's fine. I wasn't asking you anyway.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.450
What happened, Kotori?

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:14.370
It's got nothing to do with you!

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:17.290
Natsu-<i>senpai</i>!

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:18.540
Are you all right?!

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:20.750
Yasunari! You bastard!

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:23.660
Ikuto-<i>san</i>!

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:26.250
N-Natsu-<i>senpai</i>?

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:29.080
Natsusa! Don't shout
at the ground lockers like that!

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:33.200
On top of that, we're the losing team...

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:40.620
Why don't I ever get mad at my juniors?

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:43.250
It's because I immediately
snitch on them to my seniors!

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:55.040
Yasunari...

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:59.120
Hey, Yasunari.

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:02.410
You can't fight with your teammates.

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:04.750
Especially with the forwards...

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:09.950
I told you I don't need your preaching!

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:12.080
You're thinking the same thing as them!

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:16.410
The only reason I got this position
is because you're gone!

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:18.410
Yeah, I do.

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:23.200
What are you doing?!

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:27.620
Well, it takes some skill to get depressed
over something you said yourself.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.200
Are you making fun of me?!

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:31.200
No, I'm not.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:32.700
And, actually, I can tell you...

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:33.950
Huh?

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:38.160
The reason you're no good
right now, Yasunari...

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:42.790
At this rate, you're going to be
removed from the starting line-up.

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:46.410
Oh! Looks like you've already
been warned? I bet I'm right.

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:50.540
You're in such a pinch! This is bad!

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:53.830
I-I want to know...

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:56.750
Huh? What? I can't hear you.

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:58.200
I want to know!

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:02.160
Huh? Is that how you ask someone a favor?

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:04.580
Can't you speak a little more politely?

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:07.910
P-Please tell me! I'm begging you!

00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:09.370
Huh? But...

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:13.250
"Nag Nag"
Your attitude towards me has been so bad lately.

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:15.500
"Nag Nag"
I mean, you pushed me down earlier, too.

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:18.250
Look. It hurt a lot.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:20.700
Then, what do you want me to do?!

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:25.330
Will you everything I say?
For the next two weeks until the match.

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:27.660
Oh! I don't mind if you don't want to!

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:30.500
Yeah. I'm not forcing you or anything!

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:32.830
Yeah. Not at all...

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:34.790
--I'll listen.
--Huh? What?

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:36.370
I will listen to you!

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:40.540
Okay! Then, let's start with your first promise.

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:43.250
You can't fight with your teammates!

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:44.830
Especially with the forwards!

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:47.450
B-But that's because those guys--!

00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:53.290
If the forwards don't get the ball
to the backs, the backs can't do anything.

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:58.660
Fighting against people who
do that for you is stupid.

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:00.500
Promise me.

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:05.410
I promise.

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:06.870
Good boy.

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:08.910
"Doushisha Entrance"

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:12.250
"Reiwa"

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:14.830
"Reiwa"
Good morning!

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:15.700
Hello.

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:18.370
See you at the club room!

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:19.660
Huh?!

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:23.870
Did you guys just see that?!
I didn't hallucinate that, right?

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:27.120
I saw it too. Overwhelming
power harassment...

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:40.450
Protein immediately after
exercise! It's the basics!

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.580
This disgusting stuff again?!

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:47.750
What? My special protein mix is disgusting?

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:50.540
N-No...

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:57.250
Why are you holding it?
Why are you still holding it?

00:08:57.250 --> 00:09:00.120
Are you holding it because
you want to drink more of it?

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:02.250
Now. Go! Go!

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:04.080
Go! Go! You got this!

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:06.580
When it comes to guts!

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:08.750
You got it! Got it!

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:12.790
By the way, the protein I said
I liked and you responded with,

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:15.040
"Are you saying my bodybuilding is sloppy?"

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:18.200
...is in there, since you got
pissed off and didn't try it.

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:21.330
I'm very sorry.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:26.750
Oh! No! I wasn't really asking
for an apology or anything! At all!

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:31.410
Sorry about that. I guess it seemed
like pressing for something.

00:09:31.410 --> 00:09:33.870
He's on a roll today.

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:35.450
I agree.

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:39.000
Sousuke! Come on! Come on!

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:42.160
One! Two!

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:43.620
Huh?

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:46.580
Where did Natsusa and Yasunari go?

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:49.700
Oh, well. Those two are doing
some independent training.

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:50.830
Independent training?

00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:51.660
That's right.

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:54.540
Gakuto said no in the beginning,

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:57.500
but Natsusa practically got
on his knees and begged him.

00:09:57.500 --> 00:10:01.160
I spoke with our supervisor
and got it approved.

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:02.830
I see...

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:06.870
Aren't we going to practice?

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:08.910
We are.

00:10:08.910 --> 00:10:13.700
Yasunari, go through this square
and try getting from there to here.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:15.620
Don't let me touch you.

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:16.830
Huh?

00:10:16.830 --> 00:10:20.200
In other words, try to
pass me inside this box.

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:25.410
If I touch you, it means you
were tackled by the opponent.

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:29.500
People with small bodies like us

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:33.700
lose our chance at getting a try
the moment we get tackled.

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:36.160
Understand?

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:40.250
That's why we have to keep dodging
the enemies that come at us,

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:43.200
in order to carry the ball forward.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:47.120
So, let's start by practicing getting past me!

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:52.040
You think you can get by me
easily since I'm injured?

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:57.910
N-No. Shingyouji-<i>san </i>said you'd get worse
if you do intensive exercise...

00:10:57.910 --> 00:11:03.200
It's fine. Stopping you doesn't require
any intensive physical activity.

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:15.200
It's no use! I can't get past him at all!

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:17.620
Yasunari, hurry up!

00:11:17.620 --> 00:11:20.950
Actually, I can't believe you're
a starting member with skills like that.

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:23.290
No wonder you're getting removed.

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:39.660
Are you okay?!

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:40.950
I'm fine.

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:44.370
Your responsive bursts of instantaneous
power is as good as ever.

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:50.410
Hey, Yasunari. What happened to you?

00:11:50.410 --> 00:11:53.250
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:57.160
Yasunari, weren't you able
to get past me in high school?

00:11:57.160 --> 00:11:59.910
Th-There were a few times.

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:02.660
Then, why can't you get past me now?

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:06.330
On top of that, I can't move
as freely as I used to before.

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:07.660
I-I don't know.

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:10.750
Then, let me say it clearly.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:12.330
You've gotten worse.

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:17.370
Your step work is worse
than it was in high school, Yasunari.

00:12:17.370 --> 00:12:19.410
That's why your movements
are really easy to read.

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:23.370
Th-That's not true! I researched
a lot of other play styles!

00:12:23.370 --> 00:12:29.540
I studied a lot! I used what I learned
and practiced more than I did in high school!

00:12:29.540 --> 00:12:32.080
Stop doing that.

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:36.370
If you got worse after research,
study, and lots of practice...

00:12:36.370 --> 00:12:39.410
Isn't it better if you stop?

00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:43.410
But, Yasunari, you don't
have the courage to stop.

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:49.660
You ignore the fact that you keep getting
worse and hide it with wasted effort.

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:52.660
Th-Then, what more can I do?!

00:12:52.660 --> 00:12:55.120
Like I said, you don't have to do anything.

00:12:55.120 --> 00:13:01.500
Actually, you're so focused on me and your
step work that you're nearing my style.

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:04.950
You studied my plays a lot, didn't you?

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:08.540
But that's a style that only works well for me.

00:13:08.540 --> 00:13:11.290
You have your own ways of doing things.

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:13.370
You knew your own play style
back in high school.

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:18.120
Now, you don't even know what it is anymore.

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:23.120
Right now, you don't need to learn
and practice something new.

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:28.120
You need the courage to toss away
the things you thought you've gained.

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:34.200
You need to remember your own
play style and have faith in it.

00:13:44.450 --> 00:13:50.910
I think you already have the skills to stay
as a starting player. What about you?

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:55.870
If you can't believe in yourself,
I can't do anything for you.

00:13:55.870 --> 00:13:57.830
Can you believe in yourself?

00:13:57.830 --> 00:14:00.950
I-I will believe in myself.

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:01.870
Okay.

00:14:01.870 --> 00:14:03.450
Then, take out your smartphone.

00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:05.450
--Huh?
--Your smartphone. Hurry up.

00:14:05.450 --> 00:14:08.160
Um, okay.

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:13.950
Okay.

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:15.410
"Rugby"

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:16.910
"Delete"

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:20.000
Hey! Wh-What are you doing?!

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:22.410
Only look at your own plays.

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:26.120
You need to remember your
play style and practice it.

00:14:26.120 --> 00:14:29.910
How do I look at my own plays?

00:14:29.910 --> 00:14:33.660
Why don't you look at the old videos
of the matches you've played?

00:14:33.660 --> 00:14:35.660
I... I don't have anything like that.

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:38.620
What? I guess it can't be helped.

00:14:38.620 --> 00:14:42.290
Then, I'll take you to a special place of mine.

00:14:45.330 --> 00:14:47.830
Videos of Tsuru-<i>kun</i>'s matches?

00:14:47.830 --> 00:14:50.330
Yes, of course I have them.

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:52.700
Yay! Thank you! Show us!

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:55.410
"Maisagi High School"
Um, there they are.

00:14:56.950 --> 00:14:58.580
You have videos of everyone?

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:00.250
Yes, I have most of them!

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:02.120
Yuu is a fan of everyone!

00:15:02.120 --> 00:15:04.790
Yes, I am!

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:08.160
Show us the videos around Hanazono
during Yasunari's third year.

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:09.580
Okay.

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:16.200
As I thought, Yasunari was
really great during that period.

00:15:16.200 --> 00:15:21.000
He had no doubts. He had
his own sense of style...

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:22.910
What do you think, Yuu?

00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:26.830
His step work was a lot different back then!

00:15:26.830 --> 00:15:30.540
Back then, he watched the movements
of the opponent until the very last moment

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:33.700
and used the smallest number
of steps to get past them.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:39.750
But, lately, he sets up a lot of feints
and tries to confuse his opponent...

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:42.080
It's really similar to your
play style, Natsusa-<i>san</i>.

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:45.120
On top of that, you were
really good at the swerve step,

00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:47.080
but you haven't used it lately.

00:15:47.080 --> 00:15:48.160
It seems...

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:51.040
...he's gone crazy or something?

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:53.830
Oh! I'm sorry! I didn't mean
to say such cocky things!

00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:57.000
No. I agree with you completely, Yuu.

00:15:57.000 --> 00:16:00.330
He's doing too much now and
his plays are all over the place?

00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:03.910
His lack of self-confidence is showing.

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:07.000
Huh? You don't have confidence
in yourself, Tsuru-<i>kun</i>?!

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:08.370
N-Not really...

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:11.080
No way! You're such a good player!

00:16:11.080 --> 00:16:14.750
I started playing rugby
because of Natsusa-<i>san</i>,

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:17.370
but I became a fan of yours, too!

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:20.040
Especially, during Hanazono.

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:23.330
Look at this swerve! I thought it was amazing!

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:27.200
I couldn't believe someone the same
age as me could do something like this!

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:29.700
And, during this particular match--

00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:32.250
I got it. That's enough.

00:16:32.250 --> 00:16:36.250
Now, stay the night here and
research your own play style.

00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:37.410
Huh? But!

00:16:37.410 --> 00:16:39.660
I've sent the notice that you'll
be out of the dorms tonight.

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:41.080
Yuu, is that okay?

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:43.040
Yes! Of course!

00:16:43.040 --> 00:16:44.250
Wai...

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:46.120
See you later!

00:16:51.290 --> 00:16:54.410
That's really creative bullying there.

00:16:56.750 --> 00:16:59.950
He's practicing his step work
and swerves right now.

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:02.910
We're going through severe training
to get him to remember his own style.

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:05.410
He gets a ribbon every time he fails.

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:08.000
Oh, I found a good group!

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:10.950
Yasunari! Get through them!

00:17:10.950 --> 00:17:13.120
No, I think that's impossible...

00:17:13.120 --> 00:17:15.410
Huh? You want another ribbon?

00:17:15.410 --> 00:17:16.870
I'm going now.

00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:25.790
Huh?

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:28.330
He's really gotten better...

00:17:31.160 --> 00:17:34.370
Oh! Amazing! Amazing! Just a bit more!

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:39.870
You did it!

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:41.200
Yay!

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:42.790
That was amazing, Tsuru-<i>kun</i>!

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:44.370
Oh. Boo!

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:45.290
Huh?

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:48.870
I told you that getting touched
by me counts as a fail, right?

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:50.750
He's so unreasonable!

00:17:52.660 --> 00:17:54.750
I'm so tired!

00:17:57.500 --> 00:18:01.000
Didn't you get anxious when you entered college?

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:02.250
About what?

00:18:02.250 --> 00:18:05.000
No, it's fine if you didn't.

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:07.870
I did.

00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:12.750
You're scared because of how different
it is from high school, right?

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:18.750
You came to Doushisha in order to beat me,
but I was gone before you knew it.

00:18:18.750 --> 00:18:20.950
But there were people my level
all over the place here.

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:24.700
Even meeting people at
Ibuki-<i>senpai</i>'s level is pretty normal.

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:26.370
Well, of course you'd get anxious.

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:29.910
You'd wonder if you could
make it in a place like this.

00:18:29.910 --> 00:18:34.040
Yasunari, you tried to hide
that anxiety by working harder.

00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:36.040
It was the same for me, too.

00:18:36.040 --> 00:18:39.540
But, those kinds of feelings
don't disappear easily.

00:18:39.540 --> 00:18:42.040
Then, what should I do?

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:46.200
You just keep those feelings and go.

00:18:46.200 --> 00:18:50.040
But you can choose what parts
you want to focus on.

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:50.870
Huh?

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:57.540
You decide whether you focus on your
inferior qualities or superior qualities.

00:18:57.540 --> 00:19:03.040
These last few days, didn't you discover
things you are better at than others?

00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:05.410
Especially after talking with Yuu.

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:06.870
A bit...

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:11.000
Then, don't lose sight of that.
Keep honing those skills.

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:13.410
Hone them until they're super sharp.

00:19:13.410 --> 00:19:17.200
If you hone yourself into an ice pick,
you can overcome your own anxieties

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:20.580
and kill any genius with one shot.

00:19:22.580 --> 00:19:25.330
"Preseason Match"
"Doushisha University
VS
Hainokikan University"

00:19:31.450 --> 00:19:35.250
If I don't show any results today...

00:19:35.250 --> 00:19:38.290
Recover by the preseason match next week.

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:41.120
Otherwise, we'll remove you
from the starting line-up.

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:47.120
It'll be okay. It'll be okay.

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:48.250
But!

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:51.000
Should I tell you something to calm your nerves?

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:55.080
I know I should focus on my superior qualities!

00:19:55.080 --> 00:19:56.620
Even so...

00:19:56.620 --> 00:19:59.160
You don't have to be so nervous.

00:19:59.160 --> 00:20:02.290
You were just traded in for me, anyway.

00:20:02.290 --> 00:20:05.700
It's a given that you can't do better than me.

00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:11.410
That guy! He pisses me off so much!

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:16.580
Wow. Tsuru-<i>kun </i>is running so much!

00:20:20.410 --> 00:20:21.410
Shoot!

00:20:23.870 --> 00:20:27.370
Look at this swerve! I thought it was amazing!

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:31.830
I couldn't believe someone the same age
as me could do something like this!

00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:40.160
I did it!

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:43.700
No side.

00:20:43.700 --> 00:20:45.080
Good job!

00:20:45.080 --> 00:20:46.790
Yay!

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:52.620
"Doushisha"
"Team | First Half | Second Half | Total"
"Hainokikan"

00:20:53.700 --> 00:20:58.080
Good job. You ran a lot. Let's cool you down.

00:20:59.330 --> 00:21:02.200
I feel like I've gotten a bit better.

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:03.620
You're right.

00:21:03.620 --> 00:21:08.000
Let's work hard toward
the league match next week.

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:09.450
Tsuru!

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:12.950
Go on.

00:21:18.160 --> 00:21:20.160
Wh-What?

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:23.580
Thank you for giving Yasunari
a bunch of good balls.

00:21:23.580 --> 00:21:27.620
Oh, Yasunari was just unsure of himself.

00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:30.790
I thought maybe he'd go back to normal
if he gained some confidence.

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:32.450
You meddling old man.

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:37.250
I mean, we both get bullied by you.

00:21:37.250 --> 00:21:39.950
I feel a sense of closeness to him.

00:21:39.950 --> 00:21:42.200
I'm going to stab you with an ice pick.

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:44.330
Are you an assassin?

00:21:48.250 --> 00:21:50.370
...nari.

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:53.290
Yasunari...

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:55.040
Yasunari.

00:21:56.250 --> 00:21:58.620
Yes?

00:21:58.620 --> 00:22:03.540
Will you go call Sei for me?

00:22:03.540 --> 00:22:06.580
Huh? Wh-What happened?!

00:22:06.580 --> 00:22:10.620
Sorry. I don't think I can move...

00:23:41.950 --> 00:23:44.370
"A novice cook will fail at food arrangement
almost 100% of the time."
Sorry we don't appear very much.

00:23:44.370 --> 00:23:54.370
"A novice cook will fail at food arrangement
almost 100% of the time."
We won't appear next week, either. But please watch!
